s to streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["95c3d520_cd3bdbcf",66,-14,1,"This should be TypeError, but you can also use `assert_throws_js(TypeError, ...)` to simplify."],["98542370_6e0d97c8",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"piping a response into streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["a167a951_10127226",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"writing a Symbol to streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["becfb2f7_1b9d60fe",67,-14,1,"Is it a problem that close() might be called twice and that we'll then call parser->Finish() twice? I guess not, but if parser were set to null here the question wouldn't arise."],["ccf603b9_6a6df777",66,-14,1,"Can you assert that it's just a single text node with the data \"12345\"?"],["dcd29fe8_c7ef416c",66,-14,1,"\"Conflicts\" are handled in a sense. How about just: ```suggestion }, \"Interleaved streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() writes\"); ```"],["df08abc9_5c87caba",66,-14,1,"```suggestion }, \"Aborting streamAppendHTMLUnsafe()\"); ```"],["e8b92682_cd4429d2",66,-14,1,"`currentPatch` is unused."],["f8c6766e_1a9b3b87",67,-14,1,"If document.streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() is just an alias for document.documentElement.streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() and DocumentFragment doesn't work, should we really have streamAppendHTMLUnsafe() on…"],["1ee8e174_72693c83",68,-12,0,"I don't love the name, but bikeshedding is bikeshedding."],["4e010685_cddf8c30",67,-12,1,"There might need (eventually) to be a way to specify the custom element registry."],["8afd28c7_3b49d447",67,-12,1,"PErhaps this should be in the constructor instead?"],["a299bc15_6aacf135",69,-12,1,"Could use a comment here explaining what this is."],["c8133d26_dc519726",67,-12,1,"CHECKs (even though they're not DCHECKs) shouldn't have side effects that matter."]],0,392],[7166870,20410,32,0.974,0.711,[[1,1.0,306,3466]],[],0,393],[7166711,20411,10,0.354,0.243,[[0,319]],[],0,394],[7186366,20414,2,0.12,0.081,[[0,320]],[],0,395],[7209122,20424,40,0.974,0.711,[[0,0.548,321,22],[1,0.452,307,18]],[["fd5de5af_9cedcac2",70,-1,1,"Instead of a t